hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23996","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Urwah heard saying: I am Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) employed a man of Azd called Ibn al-Lutbiyyah over charity. He came and said: This is for you, and this was gifted to me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood upon the pulpit and said: What is with a worker we send, then he comes saying: This is for you, and this was gifted to me? Would he not sit in the house of his father and mother and see whether he is gifted or not? By Him in Whose hand is Muhammad's soul, none of you takes anything from it except he comes with it on the Day of Resurrection upon his neck, whether a camel with bellowing, or a cow with lowing, or a sheep bleating. Then he raised his hands until we saw the whiteness of his armpits. Then he said: O Allah, have I conveyed? Three times. And Hisham ibn Urwah added: Abu Humayd said: My ear heard and my eye saw, and ask Zayd ibn Thabit."
"23997","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far who said: Muhammad ibn Ata narrated to me, from Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi who said: I heard him while among ten of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), one of them Abu Qatadah ibn Rib'i, saying: I am most knowledgeable of you of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said to him: You were neither earliest in companionship nor most following him. He said: Yes. They said: Present. He said: When he stood to prayer, he stood upright and raised his hands until he aligned them with his shoulders. When he intended to bow, he raised his hands until he aligned them with his shoulders, then said: Allah is greatest, and bowed. Then he straightened and neither poured his head nor raised it, and placed his hands upon his knees. Then he said: Allah hears him who praises Him. Then he raised and straightened until every bone returned to its place upright. Then he went down prostrating and said: Allah is greatest. Then he kept apart and opened his upper arms from his belly, and opened the toes of his feet. Then he folded his left leg and sat upon it, and straightened until every bone returned to its place. Then he went down prostrating and said: Allah is greatest. Then he folded his leg and sat upon it until every limb returned to its place. Then he rose and did in the second rak'ah the like of that, until when he rose from the two prostrations, he uttered takbir and raised his hands until he aligned them with his shoulders, as he did when he opened the prayer. Then he did likewise, until when it was the rak'ah in which the prayer ends, he delayed his left leg and sat upon his side leaning, then gave salutation."
"23998","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Abdallah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, from Amr ibn Sulaym, that he said: Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi informed me that they said: O Messenger of Allah, how do we bless you? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say: O Allah, bless Muhammad and his wives and his offspring as You blessed the family of Ibrahim, and bless Muhammad and his wives and his offspring as You blessed the family of Ibrahim. You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"23999","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gifts of workers are misappropriation."
"24000","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abdallah ibn Isa, from Musa ibn Abdallah, from Abu Humayd or Humaydah, the doubt from Zuhayr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you proposes to a woman, there is no sin upon him to look at her, if he only looks at her for his proposal, even if she does not know."
"24001","Narrated to us Abu Kamil, narrated to us Zuhayr, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Isa, narrated to me Musa ibn Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Abu Humayd or Abu Humaydah, he said, and he had seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you proposes to a woman, there is no sin upon him to look at her if he only looks at her for his proposal, even if she does not know."
"24002","Narrated to us Affan, narrated to us Wuhayb ibn Khalid, narrated to us Amr ibn Yahya, from al-Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Saad al-Saidi, from Abu Humayd al-Saidi, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of Tabuk until we came to Wadi al-Qura, and there was a woman in her garden, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: Estimate the crop. So the people estimated, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) estimated ten awsuq, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the woman: Count what comes out of it until I return to you, if Allah wills. He said: Then he went out until he reached Tabuk, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tonight a severe wind will blow upon you, so no man among you should stand up in it, and whoever has a camel let him tie its hobble firmly. He said: Abu Humayd said: So we tied them. When it was night, a severe wind blew upon us, and a man stood up in it, so it threw him into the mountain of Tayyi. Then the king of Aylah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a white mule, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clothed him with a cloak and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote for him concerning his territory. He said: Then he turned back, and we turned back with him, until we came to Wadi al-Qura, and he said to the woman: How much was your garden? She said: Ten awsuq, the estimate of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am hastening, so whoever of you wishes to hasten, let him do so. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, and we went out with him, until when he overlooked Medina he said: This is Tabah. When he saw Uhud he said: This is Uhud, it loves us and we love it. Shall I not inform you of the best houses of the Ansar? He said: We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The best houses of the Ansar are Banu al-Najjar, then the house of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then the house of Banu Saidah, then in all the houses of the Ansar there is good."
"24003","Narrated to us Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Said, from Abu Humayd al-Saidi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a man to take the wealth of his brother without his right, and that is because of what Allah has made forbidden of the wealth of the Muslim for the Muslim."
"24004","And Ubayd ibn Abi Qurrah said: narrated to us Sulayman, narrated to me Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, narrated to me Abd al-Rahman ibn Said, from Abu Humayd al-Saidi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a man to take the staff of his brother without the goodwill of his soul, and that is because of the severity of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has made forbidden of the wealth of the Muslim for the Muslim."
"24005","Narrated to us Abu Amir, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Abd al-Malik ibn Said ibn Suwayd, from Abu Humayd and Abu Usayd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you hear a hadith from me that your hearts recognize and your hair and skin soften to it, and you see that it is close to you, then I am the most worthy of you of it. And when you hear a hadith from me that your hearts deny and your hair and skin shrink from it, and you see that it is far from you, then I am the farthest of you from it. And Ubayd ibn Abi Qurrah doubted about them and said: from Abu Humayd or Abu Usayd, and he said: you see that you are close to it. And Abu Said doubted about one of them in: when you hear a hadith from me."
"24006","Narrated to us Abu Amir, narrated to us Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Abd al-Malik ibn Said ibn Suwayd al-Ansari, he said: I heard Abu Humayd and Abu Usayd say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you enters the mosque, let him say: O Allah, open for me the doors of Your mercy. And when he goes out, let him say: O Allah, I ask You from Your bounty."
"24007","Narrated to us Rawh, narrated to us Ibn Jurayj and Zakariyya ibn Ishaq, they said: narrated to us Abu al-Zubayr, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: Abu Humayd informed me that he brought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a cup of milk from al-Naqi that was not covered, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not cover it, even with a stick you place across it. Abu Humayd said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only commanded that waterskins be tied and doors be closed at night. And Zakariyya did not mention the saying of Abu Humayd: at night."
